.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt NVRAM 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvram
.Nd read and change firmware variables
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl x | Fl X
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl d Ar name
.Op Fl r Ar name
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl s
.Op Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar value ...
.Nm
.Fl b Ar name file
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints or sets firmware variables.
A
.Ar name
alone prints that variable.
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
sets it.
.Ar name Ns += Ns Ar value
adds to its value.
.Ar name Ns -= Ns Ar value
removes from its value.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl x
Use XML for printing or reading.
Give this before
.Fl p
or
.Fl f .
.It Fl X
Use hexadecimal for printing.
Give this before
.Fl p .
.It Fl p
Print every variable.
.It Fl f Ar file
Set variables from a text file.
.It Fl d Ar name
Delete a variable, without returning an error.
.It Fl r Ar name
Delete a variable, returning an error on failure.
.It Fl c
Delete every variable.
.It Fl s
Write the changes to storage now.
.It Fl b Ar name file
Set a variable from a binary file.
This takes no other options.
.It Fl h
Print usage.
.El
